(317501, 23065, 6349, '<td valign="top">hey mav?  Enjoying the new camera?  This was a nice shot.  I gave it a 6.  Something about it just seems crooked.  It''s hard to get something like that right with the angle showing the flag and the lines of the mailbox.  Also the top part doesn''t look great cut off.  I would have stepped back one or two steps.  BTW, love the desaturation, as you know, i do it all the time.  In my opinion, this type of creative post processing doesn''t score well on here though (as can be evidenced by both my entries this week that are under 5...) oh well.  nice photo.</td>', 'hey mav?  Enjoying the new camera?  This was a nice shot.  I gave it a 6.  Something about it just seems crooked.  It''s hard to get something like that right with the angle showing the flag and the lines of the mailbox.  Also the top part doesn''t look great cut off.  I would have stepped back one or two steps.  BTW, love the desaturation, as you know, i do it all the time.  In my opinion, this type of creative post processing doesn''t score well on here though (as can be evidenced by both my entries this week that are under 5...) oh well.  nice photo.', '2003-06-06 06:43:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(317716, 23065, 6900, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments, guys.  Yes, I am enjoying the new cam, though it''s out of my hands in 3 more weeks. :(  I think this shot did well for my first submission with a different cam and for being shot 6 hrs before deadline. lol  One 1 I''ll take any day, but I''d love less 4''s and more 7''s! <br/> <br/>As for the critique - I don''t much care for borders either way.  I only border my pics because people seem to like that.  I was trying to make the arrow point to the house, but I didn''t have time to reshoot taking the top off of it, so that was a mistake, just one I failed to correct.<br/> <br/>Thanks all!</td>', 'Thanks for the comments, guys.  Yes, I am enjoying the new cam, though it''s out of my hands in 3 more weeks. :(  I think this shot did well for my first submission with a different cam and for being shot 6 hrs before deadline. lol  One 1 I''ll take any day, but I''d love less 4''s and more 7''s!  As for the critique - I don''t much care for borders either way.  I only border my pics because people seem to like that.  I was trying to make the arrow point to the house, but I didn''t have time to reshoot taking the top off of it, so that was a mistake, just one I failed to correct. Thanks all!', '2003-06-06 12:04:54.000000', NULL, 0),
